From 9c560ac5e49608baf70f519804b978cf38c6634f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joris-sta <joris-sta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:44:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] turbo3: hard-native compressed-KV flash attention tiles for
 pre-tensor-core NVIDIA GPUs

Decode path: fused per-warp decode of Turbo3 K/V inside the flash-attn
tile for Pascal (sm_61), with shape-driven dispatch (D=128/256/512,
GQA 2/4/6/8 groups of decoded rows shared across query heads, exact
six-head groups at D=256). A register-resident D=256/GQA=4 variant keeps
queries and accumulators in registers across the whole KV scan with no
shared-memory staging or CTA barriers, selectable via
GGML_CUDA_T3_DECODE_TILE=auto|scalar|warp1|warp4. Full-cache FP16
materialization is unreachable for single-token decode on this cache;
unsupported shapes abort explicitly instead of falling back.

Prefill path: small multi-token Turbo3 suffix batches (N<=4 rows,
D=128/256, masked, no ALiBi) run the same native tile
(GGML_CUDA_T3_PREFILL=auto|off|native|tile16|tile32); llama-graph packs
their strided queries so small verification batches never materialize KV.

Query rotation is applied once through the signed FWHT kernels, and an
opt-in per-operation CUDA event profiler (GGML_CUDA_PROFILE_OPS) is added
for latency diagnosis. Tensor-core GPUs keep their fused MMA path; this
native tile is the last-resort safety net for any unmatched T3 decode
shape there.

Dedicated numerical test (test-turbo3-native, 87 cases) compares
compressed CUDA decode to FP32 CPU attention over the same decoded
centroids, covering head sizes, GQA 1..32, chunked and unpadded
contexts, multiple sequences, strided views, absent masks, sinks, ALiBi
and softcapping, with and without forced CUDA graph replay.

Measured on GTX 1070 (SM 6.1): 128K-depth attention microbenchmark
8.65 -> 5.48 ms; real-model greedy-decode +15% (32K), +24% (64K),
+34% (128K) with identical output; decode +18%..+37% vs the previous
fused tile at 11K..34K context.
